### 4H.1B.2: save exam first, then try reverse writers.
### Use your own TEST course and private HTTP Client env: token, courseId.
### All successful POSTs write PostgreSQL. Choose empty test dates and keep returned IDs.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Exam 08:00-10:00 Tuesday: 201 if free.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseId": "{{courseId}}",
  "kind": "MIDTERM",
  "format": "WRITTEN",
  "startsAt": "2026-11-17T08:00:00+07:00",
  "endsAt": "2026-11-17T10:00:00+07:00",
  "timeZone": "Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh"
}

### 2. Class 09:00-11:00: expect 409 SCHEDULE_TIME_CONFLICT, kind EXAM. No insert.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/class-schedules
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseId": "{{courseId}}",
  "weekdays": [2],
  "startsOn": "2026-11-17",
  "endsOn": "2026-11-17",
  "startTime": "09:00",
  "endTime": "11:00",
  "timeZone": "Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh"
}

### 3. Class touches exam end: 201 if no other busy record.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/class-schedules
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseId": "{{courseId}}",
  "weekdays": [2],
  "startsOn": "2026-11-17",
  "endsOn": "2026-11-17",
  "startTime": "10:00",
  "endTime": "12:00",
  "timeZone": "Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh"
}

### 4. Self-study in exam: expect 409, kind EXAM. No insert.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/study-sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseId": "{{courseId}}",
  "title": "Exam conflict test",
  "startsAt": "2026-11-17T09:00:00+07:00",
  "timeZone": "Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh",
  "durationMinutes": 45
}

### Restore flow uses a DIFFERENT day. 5. Save class, record id as private offScheduleId.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/class-schedules
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseId": "{{courseId}}",
  "weekdays": [3],
  "startsOn": "2026-11-18",
  "endsOn": "2026-11-18",
  "startTime": "07:00",
  "endTime": "09:00",
  "timeZone": "Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh"
}

### 6. Get current class version. Set private offScheduleVersion from response.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/class-schedules/{{offScheduleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Cancel occurrence, 200. Record returned scheduleVersion; do not guess/increment it.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/class-schedules/{{offScheduleId}}/exceptions/2026-11-18
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "CANCELLED",
  "scheduleVersion": {{offScheduleVersion}},
  "reason": "Exam recovery test"
}

### 8. Save exam during cancelled class: 201 if otherwise free.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseId": "{{courseId}}",
  "kind": "MIDTERM",
  "format": "WRITTEN",
  "startsAt": "2026-11-18T08:00:00+07:00",
  "endsAt": "2026-11-18T10:00:00+07:00",
  "timeZone": "Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh"
}

### 9. Read fresh class version into private offScheduleVersion before restoring.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/class-schedules/{{offScheduleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Expect 409 SCHEDULE_TIME_CONFLICT, kind EXAM; cancellation/version untouched.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/class-schedules/{{offScheduleId}}/exceptions/2026-11-18?scheduleVersion={{offScheduleVersion}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Confirm cancellation still exists with the same scheduleVersion.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/class-schedules/{{offScheduleId}}/exceptions/2026-11-18
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### More Update/Change/Restore and cleanup cases: docs/BACKEND-PHASE-4H1B2.md.
### Keep tokens and private env files out of Git.
